+# S04/S05 raw-stats plan
+
+This plan prepares `C77-float-stat`, a future raw target observation package.
+It is not a Pietto SQL test, an emitter proof, a database qualification or a
+two-database differential result.
+
+## Fixed records
+
+For every applicable `(engine, function, case)`, the driver writes one JSON
+record after the future resource parent supplies an endpoint and owned output
+directory. A record includes:
+
+1. `engine`, `function`, `case`, exact raw `sql`, bound `params`, and the
+   value seed. `IN10K` is regenerated from `random.Random(72)`.
+2. An ordinal readback of the inserted seed: Int values are exact JSON
+   integers; Float values are `float.hex()` strings, including the zero sign.
+3. One normalized result-column metadata entry with `name`, `type_code` and
+   `flags`; all target warnings; and either one one-column row or a terminal
+   error containing only SQLSTATE/errno/exception type.
+4. A local judge result. `RAW_OBSERVATION` says only that the raw result meets
+   its narrow precondition; `REJECTED` retains a nonconforming primitive result.
+
+The output directory must be absent before the run. The driver creates it with
+mode 0700, creates its exact owned table, and drops that table in `finally`.
+The resource parent still owns endpoint creation, engine lock, image identity,
+session SQL mode, time ceiling, container cleanup, raw receipt and campaign
+manifest. This driver has no Docker command, default endpoint or environment
+credential lookup.
+
+## Raw SQL matrix
+
+| Pietto function | PostgreSQL primitive | MySQL Float primitive | MySQL Int reconnaissance only |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `stddev` | `STDDEV_SAMP(value)` | `STDDEV_SAMP(value)` | `STDDEV_SAMP(CAST(value AS DECIMAL(65,0)))` |
+| `variance` | `VAR_SAMP(value)` | `VAR_SAMP(value)` | `VAR_SAMP(CAST(value AS DECIMAL(65,0)))` |
+| `pvariance` | `VAR_POP(value)` | `VAR_POP(value)` | `VAR_POP(CAST(value AS DECIMAL(65,0)))` |
+| `pstdev` | `STDDEV_POP(value)` | `STDDEV_POP(value)` | `STDDEV_POP(CAST(value AS DECIMAL(65,0)))` |
